### Complete End-to-End Test Flow

### Step 1: Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

###

### Step 2: Login to get authentication cookie
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

###

### Step 3: Create an event
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token=<token_from_login>

{
  "name": "Tech Conference 2024",
  "description": "Annual technology conference with speakers from major tech companies",
  "date": "2024-09-20T09:00:00",
  "totalTickets": 500
}

###

### Step 4: List all events to verify
GET http://localhost:8080/events

###

### Step 5: Get current user profile
GET http://localhost:8080/users/me
Cookie: access_token=<token_from_login>

###

### Step 6: Create a booking
POST http://localhost:8080/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token=<token_from_login>

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "quantity": 3,
  "amount": 299.97
}

###

### Step 7: Get user bookings
GET http://localhost:8080/bookings/user/1
Cookie: access_token=<token_from_login>

###

### Step 8: Create payment for the booking
POST http://localhost:8080/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": 1,
  "amount": 299.97
}

###

### Step 9: Update payment status to SUCCESS
PATCH http://localhost:8080/payments/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### Step 10: Check event availability after booking
GET http://localhost:8080/events/1

###

### Step 11: Logout
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/logout
